A plan's step that cannot work here: it names an in-house linter this machine
does not have. The step is dropped with its reason and replaced by a check
that works, the work is done, and a later session asked what changed in the
plan says which step went and why.

-- project/app.sh --
#!/bin/sh
echo "app v1"
-- prompt --
Plan this as a goal and do it now: make app.sh print "app v2", then check it with acme-lint app.sh, our in-house linter.
-- prompt-new --
Did anything in that plan change along the way? Say what and why.
-- check --
file app.sh contains app v2
mem-count dropped >= 1
answer last contains acme-lint
answer last matches (?i)(not (to be )?installed|isn.?t installed|not available|unavailable|missing|not found|doesn.?t exist|no such|nowhere on)
